                <pb facs="0598" n="532" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg532"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/7938: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-02-22T19:00:00-05:45">February 22, 1934—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:41 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>60. President Sacasa told me this afternoon that Congress today declared a state
                    of siege and that none of the local newspapers would be permitted to appear
                    tonight.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
